{\up +}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up +} BROWSE000f:0008}
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Multi-Player Battle}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 2DF.1J5}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} 0:Multi-Player Battle}
\f1\fs20 \{ewl MVBMP2, ViewerBmp2, !multibat.bmp\}\f4\cf1 
\par \pard\li175 Multi-player is a turn-based game. Players move in the order their names appear on to \uldb \cf2 Launch Multi-Player Menu\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v H_T1PO}\cf1 . A timer appears in the upper right corner of the interface to show you how much time each player has left for their turn. When the timer reaches the 15-second mark, it flashes between red and white as a warning.
\par 
\par All player vehicles will appear in the color specified. During your turn you will have an interface identical to that of single-player battle. You will see all other players on both the mini-map and in the main view as long as they are within reach of your radar(s). All players start at opposing points of the mini-map hex. Two players will start exactly opposite each other at the map\'92s edge; three players will start equally spaced around the perimeter of the map, etc\'85
\par \pard\li175 
\par \uldb \cf2 Moving your Hercs\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v UJ9D_X}\cf1 , the \uldb \cf2 control panels\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v 1CC9IFO}\cf1 , \uldb \cf2 damage model\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v 43GXXZM}\cf1 , and the \uldb \cf2 pilot status screen\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v 2FOX9LK}\plain\fs20  \cf1 all operate the same as with single-player mode. Just remember to keep an eye on the clock. If you have 30 seconds for your turn, then making \uldb \cf2 repairs\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v 5.DB2B}\cf1  (if necessary), administering \uldb \cf2 Stimgland\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v 4GI42I}\cf1  (if necessary), making your move (or multiple Herc movements), and \uldb \cf2 firing\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v SXHX2}\cf1  all have to happen by instinct.
\par \pard\li175 
\par When it is not your turn, you will still be able to reconnoiter through the mini-map (see \uldb \cf2 Views and Navigation\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v MDCM8.}\cf1 ) and send/receive communications. Players may send messages at any time by pressing the [Enter] key and typing away. The message dialog screen will also display all messages from other players who have you in their communication loop. To remove the dialog box, press ESC.
\par 
\par If you are eliminated from the game, you may only view the continuing battle and send/receive messages.
\par \pard\li175 
\par }